cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "profilebo: Bayesian optimization of simulated trajectories toward a target profile"
abstract: >-
  Bayesian optimization of expensive simulations whose output is a trajectory
  that should follow a target profile: a POD basis of the trajectories, one
  Gaussian process per coefficient, and a composite Monte-Carlo acquisition on
  an asymmetric objective. Developed to design burnable-absorber loadings of a
  prismatic high-temperature gas-cooled reactor with Serpent 2.
authors:
  - given-names: "Nicolò"
    family-names: "Magro"
    affiliation: "Delft University of Technology"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nico7575/profilebo"
keywords:
  - Bayesian optimization
  - Gaussian processes
  - proper orthogonal decomposition
  - nuclear reactor design
  - burnable absorbers
  - Serpent
